WEBVTT

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.830
Yukishiro

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.580
Cherry blossoms bloom

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.790
Cherry blossoms bloom
And I'm so very happy

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.330
Cherry blossoms bloom
And I'm so very happy
I got to meet you!

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.170
Th-that's him, isn't it? Eiji Busujima-kun...

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.750
Looks like someone busted up
the Beast of West Middle School...

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.920
Morning! Did you oversleep again, Nanako?

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.000
Poem 1        The 5-7-5 Girl

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.540
Okay, for this problem...

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.540
Hmm... Yukishiro.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.130
Nanako Yukishiro, can you solve this one?

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.580
Oh, sorry. I forgot talking 
isn't your strong suit.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.290
You can just write out the answer
and show it to me when you're done.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.130
To tell you the truth,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.830
To tell you the truth,
I haven't quite understood

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.250
To tell you the truth,
I haven't quite understood
The last five problems...

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.880
Then say something five problems ago!

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.380
Hey Nanako-chan, how come
you always write everything down?

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.170
It's because my thoughts

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.630
It's because my thoughts
Are all jumbled and messy,

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:01.750
It's because my thoughts
Are all jumbled and messy,
So I can't speak well

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.240
Oh, I see. Limiting the words

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.500
you're able to use helps you 
keep things straight, huh?

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:09.630
Well then, what do you do when
you have to go to the bathroom?

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.460
Ah, gotcha.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.330
Nanako, did you decide what you want to eat?

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.310
One beef bowl, coming up!

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.730
How much do you want?
It's no extra charge for a bigger helping.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.380
I can pile on some more beef, if you like.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:35.880
Bigger helping...?

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.290
You want pickled ginger and an egg on top?

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.290
More beef...?

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.710
I can also do extra broth.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.210
Ginger and egg...

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:42.330
Extra broth...

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.710
It's all way too much...!

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.710
What's the matter?

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.290
Uh, she'll just have normal everything.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.210
It all worked out, huh?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.580
Y'know, Yukishiro's pretty cute...

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.330
She's so quiet and modest...

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.170
I wonder if she has a boyfriend...

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.380
Hm? What's wrong?

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.630
I just remembered

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.040
I just remembered
That I forgot to tell him

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.380
I just remembered
That I forgot to tell him
I don't like onions...

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.460
Wanna trade for my rice omelette?

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.210
The fact that she's an 
airhead is kinda cute too.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.460
I guess so...

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.750
Busujima-kun's face is all beat up again...

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.290
He's super scary. I try 
to stay away from him.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:29.500
Huh?

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.750
Huh? Whaddya want?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.540
Club meeting time already?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.960
Oh, that's right. Busujima-kun's in
the Literature Club with Nanako-chan.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.880
Why the Literature Club, of all things?

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:48.290
Dunno...

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:57.420
Hm? Oh, this?

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.580
It happened when I was playing
with my little sister yesterday!

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:06.420
She's at that irresistibly 
cute age right now!

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:11.130
Oh, I tried putting the way I was feeling
into a poem, so give it a listen.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.580
My little sister

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.960
My little sister
Is so damn adorable

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.290
My little sister
Is so damn adorable
That I could just die!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.960
How's that? Pretty proud of it, myself.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.040
You think the "I could just die!" part really
gets across just how freakin' cute she is?

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.170
I've always looked tough, so I kinda
scare people when I look at them, y'know?

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.920
What if you tried to

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.540
What if you tried to
Loosen up your mouth muscles

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:37.830
What if you tried to
Loosen up your mouth muscles
And smile a little?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.460
Oh, I get it.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.540
How's this?!

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:45.750
N-Nanako, headed to your 
club? G-good luck...!

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.500
So this is one of Nanako's friends, huh?

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.960
I oughta introduce myself.
First impressions are everything, after all...

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:59.460
It's a pleasure to meet you!
I'm Nanako's friend, Busujima.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.630
H-he's gonna pummel me!

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:05.250
Literature Club

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:12.500
Theme

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:12.540
Oh, there you are!

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.710
Reporting for duty, President Amane!

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:17.290
Well? You used to the school yet?

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:21.920
I just talked to one of my classmates
other than Nanako for the first time!

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.750
Oh, nice! What'd you talk about?

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.210
Get away! Don't touch me!

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.580
Wait! Don't run away!

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.750
That's not a conversation!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:32.330
Jeez, what are we gonna do with you?
Scaring 'em away left and right...

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.250
Oh, I know!

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.790
Why not try introducing yourself 
to people using senryu?

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:39.250
Right!

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.130
How 'bout this?

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:57.380
Hello, everyone!
How's it goin'? My name is
Eiji Busuji-

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.650
Hello, everyone!

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.050
How's it goin'? My name is

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:57.390
Eiji Busuji-

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:00.910
Hmm... I like that you stuck with the 5-7-5 format,

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.360
but you didn't even finish your name. It defeats the purpose.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:08.290
For some more info,
Make sure you head over to
My personal blog!

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.450
For some more info,

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:07.100
Make sure you head over to

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.320
My personal blog!

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:11.130
Hey, now. Quit goofing around.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.250
Hold on, you really have a blog?!

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.820
Okay then, putting Busujima's introduction aside,

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:21.080
let's write an April-themed senryu!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.580
April...

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.880
You don't have to think that hard about it.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:29.750
Just try looking at what's around you and
writing whatever pops into your head.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.130
The sky and the birds

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:36.630
The sky and the birds
Trees, forest, telephone poles,

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:37.920
The sky and the birds
Trees, forest, telephone poles,
And cherry blossoms

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.380
I didn't mean for you to list 
everything you can see...

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.210
Bust: 85-ish

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.790
Bust: 85-ish
Waist: Just over 59

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.040
Bust: 85-ish
Waist: Just over 59
Hips: 82-ish

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:52.080
P-President, is your chest really that big?!

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.750
Don't write about me! I don't count!

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.540
Man, coming up with senryu is hard...

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.000
Seriously, you're way overthinking this.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.080
When you can't come up with an idea,
try making connections.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.630
Take an image, expand upon it,
and then let the verse take shape.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:10.500
Spring

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:11.460
Entrance Ceremony - Spring

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.380
Encounter - Possible Romance - Entrance Ceremony - Spring

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.540
I get it.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:18.130
Spring

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.130
Someone Picks a Fight - Spring

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.130
Kick Their Ass - Someone Picks a Fight - Spring

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.880
Kick Their Ass Someone Else Picks a Fight 
 Kick Their Ass - Someone Picks a Fight - Spring

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.920
I'm not sure I can expand on this...

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:25.210
It's a little hard to relate to...

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.670
And a little too violent...

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:34.250
But President... you weren't scared of me
when we met, were you?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:39.040
Huh? Umm, well...

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.250
Nice to meet you! The name's Busujima!

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:48.210
I mean, I was a little nervous
the first time I saw you. But...

